# The designer handoff: the rules PDF, the 2000px logo originals and the upstream
# font packages. What the product actually ships is vendored, downscaled and
# licence-carrying under crates/k10s-assets/assets/, so nothing here is needed to
# build -- and none of it belongs in a clone.
/ui
# Local cluster credentials and the lab scratch beside them. k10s never writes
# these -- it reads the kubeconfig the environment already names -- but a lab
# that stands a cluster up next to the checkout does, and a leaked kubeconfig is
# a cluster, not a file.
kubeconfig
kubeconfig-*
*.kubeconfig
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
# Local agent instructions. Not a product file, and it does not belong in a clone.
/AGENTS.md
